  "_about": "How the report lens assembles an attack surface report for a domain or organization. sections are the lenses it runs, in order, each under its title; every lens reads the same footprint, once. findings pick the facts a lens reports that belong in the report's key findings: a fact matches when its first word is kind (or, with any_word, any of its words is), in the named lens. Key findings are listed by priority (1 first), each with how many there are and examples. The report is computed from the stored data when asked, not a live scan, and is never written to the Asset Database. Add sections and findings here, not in Go code.",
